Do you know
who you are speaking to?

462
00:39:08.041 --> 00:39:09.303
Would you like to find out?

463
00:39:10.609 --> 00:39:12.132
Hi! We're just
a couple of girls

464
00:39:12.306 --> 00:39:15.614
from Metropolis. USA.

465
00:39:15.788 --> 00:39:16.963
We're doing a fun little tour.

466
00:39:17.137 --> 00:39:18.225
Of space!

467
00:39:18.399 --> 00:39:20.445
It's for my... my birthday.

468
00:39:21.097 --> 00:39:22.098
Yeah. we've been on.
what is it.

469
00:39:22.272 --> 00:39:24.405
like. three planets so far?

470
00:39:24.579 --> 00:39:26.712
And I'm exhausted.

471
00:39:26.886 --> 00:39:29.758
You know?
Like. OMG. I had no idea

472
00:39:29.932 --> 00:39:32.065
that space was
so. like. vast and...

473
00:39:32.239 --> 00:39:33.371
Stop.

474
00:39:35.111 --> 00:39:37.418
You're hurting my head.

475
00:39:40.421 --> 00:39:42.249
You all have been
super useless.

476
00:39:43.206 --> 00:39:44.382
Happy birthday.

477
00:39:47.515 --> 00:39:48.995
Useless.

478
00:39:50.953 --> 00:39:53.608
We know friend know Brigands.

479
00:39:55.044 --> 00:39:56.611
Our house. meet?

480
00:39:56.785 --> 00:40:00.006
We walk.
but not safe for Ruthye.

481
00:40:01.094 --> 00:40:02.704
Wear this?

482
00:40:04.445 --> 00:40:07.100
Bomar get friend
and meet home.

483
00:40:30.558 --> 00:40:31.733
Wait here.

484
00:40:35.650 --> 00:40:39.045
Girl is tired. Rest.

485
00:40:39.219 --> 00:40:40.699
When will Bomar be here
with your friend?

486
00:40:40.873 --> 00:40:41.874
Soon.

487
00:40:46.008 --> 00:40:47.619
So. is Superman like you?

488
00:40:48.881 --> 00:40:51.187
Grumpy? Rude?

489
00:40:51.361 --> 00:40:53.363
- You think I'm rude?
- Of course.

490
00:40:54.190 --> 00:40:55.583
Seems to be something
you do intentionally.

491
00:40:55.757 --> 00:40:57.716
- Okay.
- Is Superman not that way?

492
00:40:57.890 --> 00:40:59.413
Clark? No.

493
00:40:59.587 --> 00:41:01.807
He's a freakin' nerd.

494
00:41:02.329 --> 00:41:03.461
Let's just say
we're not alike.

495
00:41:03.635 --> 00:41:05.680
- Because?
- I don't know.

496
00:41:05.854 --> 00:41:07.377
He sees the good in everyone.
and I see the truth.

497
00:41:07.552 --> 00:41:09.118
So you think he's naive?

498
00:41:09.292 --> 00:41:13.079
- No. but... He's young.
- But isn't he older than you?

499
00:41:13.253 --> 00:41:15.081
Yeah. but it's not his age
that makes him young.

500
00:41:15.255 --> 00:41:16.952
it's his heart.

501
00:41:17.126 --> 00:41:19.999
There are just some things
he never had to go through.

502
00:41:20.173 --> 00:41:23.263
So his heart is light.
you know?

503
00:41:23.437 --> 00:41:26.527
It's not like mine or Bomar's
or your--

504
00:41:36.189 --> 00:41:37.146
What's Earth like?

505
00:41:41.716 --> 00:41:43.239
I'm not really
from Earth. Ruthye.

506
00:41:45.067 --> 00:41:46.199
From another planet.

507
00:41:48.375 --> 00:41:49.289
Krypton.

508
00:41:53.293 --> 00:41:56.339
I thought everyone died
the day the core erupted.

509
00:41:56.905 --> 00:41:58.820
No. Krypton didn't die
in a day.

510
00:42:00.430 --> 00:42:01.693
The gods are not that kind.

511
00:42:06.785 --> 00:42:09.875
<i>My father
and his brother Jor-El</i>

512
00:42:10.049 --> 00:42:12.486
<i>tried to warn the Council
of what was coming...</i>

513
00:42:13.661 --> 00:42:16.403
<i>but no one listened.</i>

514
00:42:26.761 --> 00:42:27.849
Mm.

515
00:42:30.373 --> 00:42:32.462
Is it now?
I thought we had more time.

516
00:42:32.637 --> 00:42:35.204
So did I. but Krypton's core
is too unstable.

517
00:42:36.423 --> 00:42:37.685
It will explode in minutes.

518
00:42:38.207 --> 00:42:41.776
I have triggered
the force field. We need to go.

519
00:42:41.950 --> 00:42:43.299
Alura!

520
00:42:43.473 --> 00:42:45.432
Now!

521
00:42:53.527 --> 00:42:55.137
Is that him?

522
00:42:57.705 --> 00:42:58.663
That is Kal-El.

523
00:42:58.880 --> 00:43:00.316
The sweet little boy

524
00:43:00.490 --> 00:43:01.622
your brother has declared
a conqueror of worlds.

525
00:43:06.322 --> 00:43:07.933
It's time.

526
00:43:44.534 --> 00:43:47.146
<i>That was eight years
before I was born.</i>

527
00:43:59.767 --> 00:44:02.727
Are we fools. Zor-El?

528
00:44:02.901 --> 00:44:06.121
Should we have listened
to your brother?

529
00:44:06.295 --> 00:44:09.081
We can't send our daughter...

530
00:44:09.255 --> 00:44:11.431
to another planet
to be some sort of god.

531
00:44:11.910 --> 00:44:13.651
We preserved all this
for a reason.

532
00:44:15.740 --> 00:44:19.700
We have to believe
there's a future here.

533
00:44:26.315 --> 00:44:29.101
Kara. where are you?

534
00:44:38.458 --> 00:44:40.721
<i>Honestly. I didn't have a clue</i>

535
00:44:40.895 --> 00:44:44.551
<i>that Argo was different
from any other planet.</i>

536
00:44:46.466 --> 00:44:47.728
<i>I thought we were lucky.</i>

537
00:44:49.425 --> 00:44:51.601
<i>But luck.
almost by definition.</i>

538
00:44:51.776 --> 00:44:52.690
<i>runs out.</i>

539
00:45:02.830 --> 00:45:03.701
Tell me.

540
00:45:05.964 --> 00:45:08.706
When Argo City broke off.
it unearthed...

541
00:45:08.880 --> 00:45:12.927
a crystalline mineral
buried deep in the planet.

542
00:45:14.146 --> 00:45:14.799
Kryptonite.

543
00:45:16.409 --> 00:45:19.151
The soil has been poisoned.

544
00:45:19.542 --> 00:45:22.154
People are ill all over Argo...

545
00:45:22.371 --> 00:45:24.852
and it's spreading.

546
00:45:26.636 --> 00:45:29.509
And can it be helped?

547
00:45:46.439 --> 00:45:46.831
Kara.

548
00:45:48.833 --> 00:45:49.921
What is all this?

549
00:45:52.140 --> 00:45:56.188
Trying to preserve Argo with
my force field was a failure.

550
00:45:57.189 --> 00:46:01.019
The radiation
has taken hold of me. too.

551
00:46:03.064 --> 00:46:04.674
I cannot let it get you.

552
00:46:08.809 --> 00:46:11.551
I found my brother's sketches
for the escape pod.

553
00:46:12.726 --> 00:46:14.075
I made it big enough for you.

554
00:46:15.947 --> 00:46:18.166
You will follow your cousin.
Kal-El.

555
00:46:19.820 --> 00:46:22.649
You will make a new home
on Earth.

556
00:46:25.478 --> 00:46:26.218
No!

557
00:46:27.915 --> 00:46:29.003
This is my home.

558
00:46:29.917 --> 00:46:33.529
This is my only home.

559
00:46:36.184 --> 00:46:38.883
Let the radiation take me too.

560
00:46:39.666 --> 00:46:43.322
I'll lie in the ground
next to you and next to mom.

561
00:46:47.065 --> 00:46:49.154
I am one tiny life.

562
00:46:50.285 --> 00:46:53.941
What difference does it make
whether I live or die?

563
00:46:54.115 --> 00:46:57.075
You are not one tiny life.

564
00:46:58.206 --> 00:47:01.035
You are your mother's life.

565
00:47:02.297 --> 00:47:03.951
You are my life.

566
00:47:05.431 --> 00:47:08.826
You are our souls
unfolding into the future.

567
00:47:10.175 --> 00:47:11.480
My child...

568
00:47:12.133 --> 00:47:14.832
this is why you must live.

569
00:47:27.496 --> 00:47:29.107
When I am gone.

570
00:47:30.717 --> 00:47:34.242
I need you
to promise me something.

571
00:47:35.156 --> 00:47:36.244
Of course. mother.

572
00:47:38.159 --> 00:47:40.379
Just be good.

573
00:47:40.553 --> 00:47:44.862
That doesn't mean
you cannot be tough.

574
00:47:45.036 --> 00:47:47.995
And that doesn't mean
you have to be nice.

575
00:47:50.476 --> 00:47:52.304
But you must be good.

576
00:48:01.617 --> 00:48:04.011
We do not choose our paths.

577
00:48:06.144 --> 00:48:08.537
Your path
will be one of great effort...

578
00:48:10.888 --> 00:48:13.107
of great purpose.

579
00:48:15.283 --> 00:48:20.114
Where you are going.
you will have enormous power.

580
00:48:21.986 --> 00:48:23.248
Use it to protect those...

581
00:48:23.422 --> 00:48:25.380
who cannot protect themselves.

582
00:48:27.165 --> 00:48:29.036
Trust yourself...

583
00:48:29.471 --> 00:48:30.733
to know what is right. Kara.

584
00:49:12.645 --> 00:49:13.863
We are with you.

585
00:49:48.376 --> 00:49:49.377
So. yeah.

586
00:49:52.337 --> 00:49:53.555
When I say
I know what it's like.

587
00:49:53.729 --> 00:49:55.557
I'm not talking
out of my ass. Ruthye.

588
00:49:55.731 --> 00:49:57.559
Grief is a killer. You know?

589
00:49:57.733 --> 00:49:59.300
It can make you want
to break bad. or...

590
00:50:00.693 --> 00:50:02.216
you know. get revenge. but...

591
00:50:05.828 --> 00:50:07.134
I don't think
any of those things

592
00:50:07.308 --> 00:50:08.701
are gonna lead you
to where you want to go.

593
00:50:12.705 --> 00:50:13.662
So. what does?

594
00:50:15.577 --> 00:50:17.231
When did you stop
feeling angry?

595
00:50:19.581 --> 00:50:21.018
Any day now.

596
00:50:37.338 --> 00:50:38.731
Um...

597
00:50:38.905 --> 00:50:40.211
I'm just gonna
go check on him.

598
00:50:41.212 --> 00:50:42.604
Stay here.

599
00:51:12.547 --> 00:51:13.548
Where's your friend?

600
00:51:13.722 --> 00:51:15.768
They come now. Sit.

601
00:51:29.695 --> 00:51:32.263
Recipe from my mother.

602
00:51:32.437 --> 00:51:34.221
from her mother.
mother. mother...

603
00:51:35.962 --> 00:51:38.617
- A little bitter.
- Thank you.

604
00:51:39.661 --> 00:51:40.662
Drink.

605
00:51:52.109 --> 00:51:53.284
How does your friend
know the Brigands?

606
00:51:55.851 --> 00:51:58.245
We all know the Brigands.

607
00:52:00.595 --> 00:52:01.770
But you said--

608
00:52:01.944 --> 00:52:04.904
Brigands come here.
take girls.

609
00:52:05.078 --> 00:52:08.125
They come here.
take... our girl.

610
00:52:10.692 --> 00:52:11.737
Sarna.

611
00:52:13.391 --> 00:52:16.481
Yeah. your. um...
your daughter. the...

612
00:52:17.308 --> 00:52:18.613
The pictures.

613
00:52:21.050 --> 00:52:22.617
What did you give me?

614
00:52:23.618 --> 00:52:25.403
Sorry. Sorry. stop drinking.
Stop drinking.

615
00:52:25.577 --> 00:52:26.926
Bomar. stop!

616
00:52:27.100 --> 00:52:28.884
It's for our daughter.
we have no choice.

617
00:52:29.058 --> 00:52:30.756
Did you get
this poison from the Brigands?

618
00:52:30.930 --> 00:52:33.976
I-- No understand.
You should be...

619
00:52:34.151 --> 00:52:35.804
Paralyzed.

620
00:52:35.978 --> 00:52:37.502
This is just
really gonna suck.

621
00:52:39.939 --> 00:52:41.245
Ow.

622
00:52:43.595 --> 00:52:44.900
Whoa.

623
00:52:49.340 --> 00:52:50.950
- Milk.
- Why?

624
00:52:51.124 --> 00:52:53.735
Well. it coats your stomach
if you've been poisoned.

625
00:52:53.909 --> 00:52:55.041
Come on. man.

626
00:52:55.215 --> 00:52:56.608
It's a white liquid.

627
00:52:56.782 --> 00:52:58.044
- Door. Door.
- Help me out here.

628
00:53:06.661 --> 00:53:07.880
What kind of milk
was that?

629
00:53:08.054 --> 00:53:09.055
Chewchan.

630
00:53:09.838 --> 00:53:10.926
Chewchan.

631
00:53:11.100 --> 00:53:12.928
Oh. my God. Okay.

632
00:53:13.625 --> 00:53:15.104
So. you sold me out...
for what?

633
00:53:15.279 --> 00:53:17.281
What are you... What are you
getting in return?

634
00:53:17.455 --> 00:53:18.630
Speak.

635
00:53:19.152 --> 00:53:21.502
One girl for two girls.

636
00:53:54.187 --> 00:53:55.188
Hello.

637
00:53:59.148 --> 00:54:00.149
Are you okay?

638
00:54:03.849 --> 00:54:05.590
I heard
you were looking for me.

639
00:54:05.764 --> 00:54:07.026
Huh?

640
00:54:09.420 --> 00:54:10.769
You found me.

641
00:54:10.943 --> 00:54:12.684
Technically. you found me.

642
00:54:23.825 --> 00:54:25.044
Mm.

643
00:54:40.233 --> 00:54:42.801
Hey. man. Can you just give me
one second?

644
00:54:53.681 --> 00:54:55.640
Thanks. I needed that.

645
00:55:11.786 --> 00:55:14.963
You dropped
your puppy's antidote.

646
00:55:19.316 --> 00:55:20.186
Kara!

647
00:55:22.797 --> 00:55:24.103
Help me!

648
00:55:26.410 --> 00:55:27.498
Help!

649
00:55:30.805 --> 00:55:32.285
No!

650
00:55:33.721 --> 00:55:34.592
Kara!

651
00:55:42.513 --> 00:55:43.905
Come on!

652
00:55:51.304 --> 00:55:52.392
Whoa!

653
00:55:55.090 --> 00:55:56.265
Sorry!

654
00:55:59.268 --> 00:56:00.618
- Are you drunk?
- No!

655
00:56:06.101 --> 00:56:07.755
Hey.

656
00:56:07.929 --> 00:56:09.757
She don't look very poisoned
to me. eh?

657
00:56:11.672 --> 00:56:12.456
Bring me their daughter.

658
00:56:12.630 --> 00:56:13.892
Now.

659
00:56:14.501 --> 00:56:15.589
You smell of vomit.

660
00:56:15.763 --> 00:56:17.112
Because Mareck poisoned me.

661
00:56:17.983 --> 00:56:20.115
Oh. and I am fine.
thank you for asking.

662
00:56:40.658 --> 00:56:41.572
Huh.

663
00:56:48.448 --> 00:56:49.841
The brides!

664
00:56:50.015 --> 00:56:50.885
Get them! Get them!

665
00:56:54.933 --> 00:56:55.934
Don't move.

666
00:57:30.055 --> 00:57:31.012
Run.

667
00:57:44.373 --> 00:57:45.853
Drom Baxton.

668
00:57:46.637 --> 00:57:48.377
There's a lot of rich dipshits
looking for you.

669
00:57:48.552 --> 00:57:49.944
Screw you. old man.

670
00:57:52.556 --> 00:57:53.731
Shit.

671
00:58:06.787 --> 00:58:09.094
- Sarna! Sarna!
- Sarna! Sarna! Sarna!

672
00:58:09.268 --> 00:58:10.487
A deal is a deal.

673
00:58:11.575 --> 00:58:12.793
She has to die.

674
00:58:12.967 --> 00:58:14.229
- No!
- Sarna!

675
00:58:33.553 --> 00:58:34.815
Ouch.

676
00:58:43.215 --> 00:58:43.781
Aren't you the ditz
from that dive bar?

677
00:58:43.955 --> 00:58:45.086
Funny.

678
00:58:46.435 --> 00:58:47.349
That's what
I've been calling you.

679
00:58:47.524 --> 00:58:48.437
Touché!

680
00:59:53.938 --> 00:59:55.722
Oh. that's ballsy.

681
00:59:55.896 --> 00:59:58.420
Drom Baxton!
You just made me angry.

682
01:00:08.909 --> 01:00:09.823
Got you. bastich.

683
01:00:19.746 --> 01:00:21.356
Sarna.

684
01:00:23.358 --> 01:00:25.447
Where are you?

685
01:00:26.013 --> 01:00:28.189
You okay? Yeah?
Okay. get her out of here.

686
01:00:28.363 --> 01:00:30.627
She's the last one. Go. Go!

687
01:00:45.729 --> 01:00:48.514
Come on. Krem.
Where's my antidote?

688
01:00:49.254 --> 01:00:50.908
You like to play games.

689
01:00:52.170 --> 01:00:54.085
I can play games.

690
01:01:01.048 --> 01:01:04.095
I can smell you.

691
01:01:23.027 --> 01:01:24.245
- I told you not to move.
- I had him.

692
01:01:24.419 --> 01:01:25.594
Hide.

693
01:01:31.557 --> 01:01:32.514
Shit!

694
01:01:35.126 --> 01:01:36.040
Sarna!

695
01:01:39.913 --> 01:01:41.132
Bye-bye.

696
01:01:41.741 --> 01:01:43.308
No! No!

697
01:02:16.297 --> 01:02:17.864
They're dead.

698
01:02:18.038 --> 01:02:20.084
Because you did not let me do
what had to be done!

699
01:02:20.258 --> 01:02:22.260
Okay. Ruthye. I'm not
letting you kill that man.

700
01:02:22.434 --> 01:02:24.871
Why not? Look at the suffering
he leaves in his wake.

701
01:02:25.045 --> 01:02:26.568
Why does he get to be alive?
Why?

702
01:02:26.743 --> 01:02:28.483
Okay! Okay. stop freaking out!

703
01:02:28.657 --> 01:02:31.922
Get off! Don't tell me
not to freak out.

704
01:02:32.096 --> 01:02:33.619
I'm allowed.

705
01:02:33.793 --> 01:02:34.968
Tell me why.

706
01:02:35.142 --> 01:02:36.753
Because it'll mess you up.

707
01:02:37.275 --> 01:02:39.756
You think it will make you
feel better? It won't.

708
01:02:40.234 --> 01:02:42.062
It'll haunt you
for the rest of your life.

709
01:02:42.236 --> 01:02:43.368
Is that what you want?

710
01:02:45.544 --> 01:02:47.024
So. the alternative
is to be like you?

711
01:02:48.199 --> 01:02:49.722
Constantly leaving your planet

712
01:02:49.896 --> 01:02:50.767
to drink yourself
into a stupor?

713
01:02:52.029 --> 01:02:53.291
Drunk all of the time

714
01:02:53.465 --> 01:02:55.075
so you never
have to feel anything?

715
01:02:55.249 --> 01:02:57.861
Guess what? I too want
to free myself of this pain.

716
01:02:58.383 --> 01:02:59.732
And I do not want
to be like you.

717
01:03:00.864 --> 01:03:01.821
Okay.

718
01:03:03.301 --> 01:03:04.781
Then why don't you go find

719
01:03:04.955 --> 01:03:06.565
whatever dimensional portal
he just passed through

720
01:03:06.739 --> 01:03:08.132
all by yourself?

721
01:04:29.430 --> 01:04:30.649
Hey! Squidward!

722
01:04:30.823 --> 01:04:31.780
Where are the Brigands?

723
01:04:31.955 --> 01:04:33.565
- No idea.
- Really?

724
01:04:33.739 --> 01:04:35.654
- Aargh!
- Bullshit.

725
01:04:35.828 --> 01:04:38.439
I have less than 24 hours
to save my dog.

726
01:04:38.613 --> 01:04:40.311
so you tell me
where the Brigands are

727
01:04:40.485 --> 01:04:42.966
and I won't turn you
into a hand puppet. Okay?

728
01:04:43.140 --> 01:04:44.228
Okay.

729
01:04:49.189 --> 01:04:52.801
Okay.
But you'll have to wear this.

730
01:04:58.633 --> 01:04:59.765
Let's go.

731
01:05:35.235 --> 01:05:36.715
This is as close as we get.

732
01:06:46.524 --> 01:06:47.525
Hi. there.

733
01:06:50.528 --> 01:06:52.008
I've been tracking your ship
for the last month.

734
01:06:52.182 --> 01:06:54.314
I believe you're from Krypton?

735
01:06:54.488 --> 01:06:55.446
And so am I.

736
01:06:57.317 --> 01:06:58.710
Clark.

737
01:06:59.798 --> 01:07:00.799
I don't understand you.

738
01:07:01.582 --> 01:07:02.975
Where am I?

739
01:07:03.280 --> 01:07:05.108
Is this Earth?

740
01:07:06.326 --> 01:07:07.719
Are you Kal-El?

741
01:07:07.893 --> 01:07:09.590
I'm sorry. I don't...

742
01:07:09.764 --> 01:07:10.635
I don't. um...

743
01:07:11.766 --> 01:07:12.767
I don't speak Kryptonian.

744
01:07:12.941 --> 01:07:14.160
I didn't ever...

745
01:07:14.943 --> 01:07:17.294
Shoot. I...
I wasn't raised there. so...

746
01:07:17.468 --> 01:07:18.382
I wasn't raised there!

747
01:07:18.556 --> 01:07:19.426
Why am I talking louder?

748
01:07:19.600 --> 01:07:21.167
Let me help you.

749
01:07:21.341 --> 01:07:22.516
Krypto. be good. buddy.

750
01:07:23.430 --> 01:07:24.736
Be good.

751
01:07:24.910 --> 01:07:26.042
He's a feisty little guy.

752
01:07:26.216 --> 01:07:27.260
He's cute.

753
01:07:28.479 --> 01:07:29.480
Is it okay if I...

754
01:07:34.833 --> 01:07:35.790
Watch your step there.

755
01:07:36.791 --> 01:07:38.402
Might be slippery. so...

756
01:07:38.576 --> 01:07:40.404
Is this... I'll grab it.

757
01:07:42.014 --> 01:07:43.015
Okay.

758
01:07:44.234 --> 01:07:46.062
Ah. yeah. Pretty cool. huh?

759
01:07:48.412 --> 01:07:50.327
Don't worry.
we don't actually live here.

760
01:07:50.892 --> 01:07:52.633
There's a lot more to Earth
than just this place.

761
01:07:53.982 --> 01:07:55.984
Big city. Lots of stuff to do.

762
01:07:56.159 --> 01:07:57.943
Bowling. that's fun.

763
01:07:58.117 --> 01:07:59.553
It was a big adjustment
for me.

764
01:07:59.727 --> 01:08:01.033
You know. coming from Kansas.

765
01:08:01.207 --> 01:08:02.817
You know.
small town kinda guy. but...

766
01:08:02.991 --> 01:08:04.341
You know Kansas?

767
01:08:04.515 --> 01:08:06.082
No. Why would you know Kansas?

768
01:08:06.256 --> 01:08:08.736
What am I...?

769
01:08:08.910 --> 01:08:10.738
You can't understand a word
that I'm saying right now.

770
01:08:12.958 --> 01:08:15.352
It's okay. You will one day.

771
01:08:15.874 --> 01:08:18.485
And you'll also learn to love
this place just like I have.

772
01:08:19.573 --> 01:08:20.531
Promise.

773
01:08:24.448 --> 01:08:26.189
Why is he in his underwear?

774
01:08:26.363 --> 01:08:27.712
Oh.
Should mention.

775
01:08:29.931 --> 01:08:32.978
Your powers are gonna start
kicking in right about...

776
01:08:33.152 --> 01:08:34.197
now.

777
01:08:48.820 --> 01:08:50.430
How can this be home?

778
01:09:56.104 --> 01:09:57.410
I thought that the shelter
might help.

779
01:09:58.106 --> 01:09:59.064
Was I right?

780
01:09:59.238 --> 01:10:00.152
Wait...

781
01:10:01.153 --> 01:10:02.285
What did you...

782
01:10:02.459 --> 01:10:03.677
I saw you boarding
that man's ship.

783
01:10:03.851 --> 01:10:05.157
so I snuck up
into the cargo hold.

784
01:10:06.289 --> 01:10:07.333
What's this place?

785
01:10:11.511 --> 01:10:13.426
It's my prison.

786
01:10:13.600 --> 01:10:16.734
The Brigands know that
the planet orbits between...

787
01:10:17.691 --> 01:10:18.779
two suns.

788
01:10:20.477 --> 01:10:21.913
And that the green sun...

789
01:10:23.480 --> 01:10:24.437
can kill me.

790
01:10:28.485 --> 01:10:30.922
Krem left your ship on Bilquis
and I found this.

791
01:10:32.967 --> 01:10:34.186
Thought that it might help.

792
01:10:37.885 --> 01:10:40.671
It's... It's just
a stupid suit. Ruthye.

793
01:10:43.369 --> 01:10:45.328
It doesn't do anything.

794
01:10:56.339 --> 01:10:57.905
My dog...

